      "extract": "Introduction It has long been hoped that the fundamental particles, of which all matter in the Universe is composed, would turn out to be topological structures of some type. This prospect is appealing because if correct it would indicate that the permanence of matter and its properties (obeying principles like the conservation of electric charge) could be explained in terms of diﬀerent topological classes, which",
